<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly firmer in New York, Dow up 76 pts.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly firmer in New York, Dow up 76 pts.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs finished mostly stronger in New York trade, where the Dow Industrials Index ended 76.19 points higher at 6,625.67.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia at 11.15 a.m. (2215 GMT).</p>
<p>Company     Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$17 3/4	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$32 1/8	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$29 1/2	   nil</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$20 3/4	 +0 1/4</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16 1/2	 -0 1/8</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$85	     +1 7/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33 1/2		nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  28		 untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  239 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  148 1/2	   -1 3/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  137 3/4	   +1 1/2</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.16	   untraded</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.63	   untraded</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.70	   untraded</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
